Description: screen mirroring receiver for AirPlay, Google Cast, Miracast and DLNA
 AirShow turns a computer or a single-board computer attached to a display
 into a receiver that phones, tablets and laptops can mirror their screens
 to. It shows a fullscreen idle screen until a sender connects.
 .
 It accepts AirPlay screen mirroring from iOS and macOS, Google Cast
 mirroring from Chrome and Android, Miracast from Windows and Android, and
 media pushed by DLNA controllers.
 .
 It also includes airshow-kiosk and systemd user units that run AirShow
 underneath a fullscreen kiosk browser and hide the browser while someone
 is casting; see /usr/share/doc/airshow/README.kiosk.md.
